@@ -0,0 +1,660 @@
+From: Akhilesh Samineni <akhilesh.samineni@broadcom.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: add SONiC fullcone NAT with isolated reservations
+
+Based on SONiC fullcone NAT and openwrt-sonic-fullcone revision
+4de0643f6b48e7e7d57d768144204ce5d3078c8f. Use conntrack-owned bindings,
+not an xtables mapping table or a separate garbage collection worker.
+
+Serialize fullcone mapping reuse by internal endpoint. Check and publish
+translated endpoints under the translated bucket lock, also used for
+removal. Ordinary NAT participates in reservations but is never exposed
+by fullcone DNAT. Include network namespace, both zone directions and
+address family in matching. Only confirmed live fullcone bindings may
+receive new inbound peers; existing flows retain normal flowtable/PPE
+eligibility. Retry competing reservations with a bounded allocation cost
+and drop instead of replacing a live mapping.
+
+Keep ordinary NAT allocator fallback behavior. Fullcone is limited to
+TCP, UDP, UDP-Lite and SCTP; other protocols and helper-managed flows
+retain ordinary NAT semantics. Mapping lifetime follows outbound
+conntracks, including references held by flowtable offload.
+
+Protect source reuse, inbound lookup and reservation checks against object
+recycling with their list bucket locks. A matching endpoint owner suffices
+to decide sharing; compile out all added state when fullcone is disabled.
+
+Signed-off-by: Akhilesh Samineni <akhilesh.samineni@broadcom.com>
+
